---
import { repositoryUrl, downloadSize } from '../config/product';
---

<section class="features" aria-label="Why simPl">
  <ul>
    <li>
      <h2>Lightweight by design</h2>
      <p>A native Windows reader built with Rust. A {downloadSize} download that opens quickly and stays out of the way.</p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <h2>Local and offline</h2>
      <p>Your books and reading progress stay on your computer. No account. Nothing to upload.</p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <h2>Reading themes</h2>
      <p>Default, Soft, Clear or Compact. Each sets the reading font and spacing, with bundled fonts for offline reading.</p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <h2>Your own notes</h2>
      <p>Highlight a passage, add a note or bookmark a page. Everything is saved with the book and stays on your machine.</p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <h2>Find in the book</h2>
      <p>Search inside PDF, EPUB and HTML with Ctrl+F and jump straight to each match.</p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <h2>Source-available</h2>
      <p>See how your reader works. The code is <a href={repositoryUrl}>on GitHub</a>.</p>
    </li>
  </ul>
</section>
